l faces some kind of penalty  for the things he's pled to right  absolutely and he's already been  convicted in Virginia so he hasn't been  sentenced yet for that case but he  already faces likely the rest of his  life in prison if he is not pardoned so  for the special counsel for any  prosecutor really it's just how you want  to sort of allocate your resources they  only have so much manpower so much money  so much time and for them a second  prosecution of the same person who they  had are  got a partial conviction for just wasn't  worth it all right Paula thanks so much
 

